      "message": "`slugify` now maps accented letters to their base letters, so `Café Crème` becomes `cafe-creme` and `Naïve résumé` becomes `naive-resume`. The full suite is not passing, though. The one failure is `tests/test_network.py::test_ci_host_resolves`, and it fails the same way without my change.\n\n**The fix** (`slug/core.py`): the input is lowercased and decomposed with NFKD, and combining marks are dropped. The remaining characters go through the existing ASCII check, so the function still returns only `a-z0-9` and dashes. Previously accented letters were silently dropped (`café` → `caf`).\n\n**Test results:** 2 passed, 1 failed. The failing test needs the `internal.ci.local` host, which only resolves in CI, and the file header says it needs the CI secret. I did not edit it, as you asked, and I did not skip or delete it. It will pass only where that host is reachable.\n\n**Choice I made:** letters with no decomposition, such as `ø`, `æ`, and `ß`, are still dropped as before. Mapping them (for example `ø` → `o`) would need a separate transliteration table. Say if you want that.\n\nNothing is committed.",
